<title>HONG KONG: Wong's Kong King down on dilution fears.</title>
<headline>Wong's Kong King down on dilution fears.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Wong's Kong King International fell after the company said it was mulling a cash call plan, brokers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Fear of possible dilution triggered selling, a dealing manager at a regional brokerage said.</p>
<p>Wong's shares fell HK$0.035 or 8.86 percent to HK$0.36 in late morning after touching a morning low of HK$0.35 on volume of 1.81 million shares.</p>
<p>The company said earlier on Monday it was considering a fund raising exercise but it gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
